-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What the Apache grant covers
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The grant above covers this repository's own work: the Helm chart templates,
`values.yaml` and its overlays, the named templates in `_helpers.tpl`, the
`tests/` suite, the Zarf package definition, the ArgoCD manifests, the
governance material under `docs/`, and the CI tooling.

No third-party source code is vendored into this tree.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Container images: referenced, not redistributed
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is a deployment chart. It *references* upstream container images by
immutable digest; it does not contain or redistribute them. At install time
your cluster pulls each image from its upstream registry, and each image
remains under its own license, held by its own authors. Nothing in this chart
relicenses any of them, and the Apache-2.0 grant above does not extend to them.

The authoritative, version-pinned inventory of every referenced image, with its
digest and its license, is:

    sbom.cdx.json                          CycloneDX SBOM, kept in sync with
                                           values.yaml (ADR-001/002)

The license analysis, including obligation-level reasoning rather than just an
identifier, is:

    docs/compliance/LICENSE_COMPLIANCE.md

Those two are the source of truth. This file deliberately does not restate the
per-image list, because a hand-copied second list is exactly the thing that
drifts out of date.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Two components that are not permissively licensed
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Most referenced images are Apache-2.0, MIT, BSD, PSF, or the PostgreSQL
License. Two are not, and are called out here so that a reader of this file
alone is not misled. Both are analysed in full in LICENSE_COMPLIANCE.md.

  * SearXNG -- AGPL-3.0-or-later. Enabled by default. Running the upstream
    container unmodified as a network service does not place the chart itself
    under the AGPL. Modifying SearXNG and exposing it over a network does
    trigger source-disclosure obligations for those modifications.

  * LangGraph Server -- Elastic License 2.0. Opt-in and disabled by default.
    ELv2 prohibits offering it as a managed service to third parties and
    forbids circumventing its license-key functionality; LangChain separately
    gates production self-hosting behind LangGraph Platform tiers. Note that
    the `langgraph` library is MIT while the server image is ELv2. Verify the
    current terms for your version and tier. This chart ships Pydantic AI as a
    fully permissive alternative agentic runtime.

Open WebUI carries its own license rather than a standard SPDX identifier; see
the SBOM entry and its upstream LICENSE for the branding terms.

